# The Problem

Long chains of `else if` can be hard to read:

```csharp
if (direction == "north") { ... }
else if (direction == "south") { ... }
else if (direction == "east") { ... }
else if (direction == "west") { ... }
else { Debug.Log("Invalid"); }
```

A **switch** statement cleans this up by checking a single variable against many possible values.

slides.codeSnippet:
switch (variable)
{
    case value1:
        // code
        break;
    case value2:
        // code
        break;
    default:
        // if no case matched
        break;
}

void OnTriggerEnter(Collider other)
{
    string tag = other.tag;
    switch (tag)
    {
        case "Coin":
            AddCoins(1);
            break;
        case "HealthPack":
            Heal(25);
            break;
        case "PowerUp":
            ActivatePowerUp();
            break;
        default:
            Debug.Log("Unknown item collected");
            break;
    }
}
